    "result_text": "The full suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). There is a single test class, `AcceptanceTest`, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`, YY = last two digits of the registrationDate year) with minimal structural impact \u2014 **2 files touched, no method grown**:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `membershipNumber` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a single `@Mapping` expression to the existing `toOwnerDto` declaration. Following the file's own idiom (the neighboring `displayName` expression mapping), it derives the value straight from the owner's fields:\n   ```java\n   owner.getCustomerCode() + \"-M\" + String.format(\"%02d\", owner.getRegistrationDate().getYear() % 100)\n   ```\n   It null-guards on `customerCode`/`registrationDate`, so seed owners (which have both columns `NULL` in `data.sql`) serialize as `membershipNumber: null` rather than throwing.\n\nI deliberately avoided adding a method to the large `Owner` entity (high surrounding complexity \u2014 every other method's CC would be paid for), placing the derivation instead in the small `OwnerMapper` interface where the surrounding context is cheap.",
